Description:
    Adds a has_one_attached upload onto a resource that
    hibiki:rails:scaffold_controller already generated, on both edit
    surfaces. One attachment per run.

    The classic form gains a direct-upload file field plus a remove
    checkbox (a virtual remove_<attachment> attribute on the model, whose
    purge yields to a same-submit upload). The inline channel form gains a
    nameless file input that direct-uploads on change and hands only the
    signed blob id to the graph — the pending state lives there, keyed by
    the form's dom, so it survives repaints and the edit row and inline
    create form stay independent.

    The channel gains one `include`; everything else lives in a generated
    concern under app/channels/concerns that wraps the lifecycle with
    super. Both channel queries are preloaded with with_attached_<name>,
    and one shared upload_field_controller.js is emitted per app.

    --accept=pdf,doc narrows the file inputs (image by default; tokens
    image, audio, video, pdf, csv, text, doc, xls, ppt, or a raw
    type/subtype or .ext). Images render as thumbnails, anything else as
    its filename and size — decided per blob at render time, so mixed
    lists work and a wrong-typed file never breaks the page.

    Prerequisites (warned about, never installed): the Active Storage
    tables, the image_processing gem for thumbnails (when images are
    accepted), and ActiveStorage.start() in the JS entrypoint for the
    classic form.

Examples:
    bin/rails g hibiki:rails:upload_field Album cover

    bin/rails g hibiki:rails:upload_field Report document --accept=pdf,doc

    bin/rails g hibiki:rails:upload_field Album cover --css=tailwind --phlex
